Yea, but you can not do that with root, as it is not allowed to 
have more than one volume.  

More than one volume became a chicken and the egg problem during 
boot, especially if the files you needed to boot from were split 
across multiple volumes.  Or worse, the single boot device you get 
to specify to the firmware did not have the /etc/fdmns directory, 
or it wasn't where the /dev directory was.

Soooo, the AdvFS root volume can ONLY have a single disk.

Otherwise addvol/rmvol is wonderful.

                                        Bob Harris


