On 31 srp, 20:59, pear...@aol.com wrote:
> However we still would like to use dd to remote tape.

Mybe this will help:

-doing a tar to remote tape via ssh:

tar cpfv - /src_dir | ssh remote_host "/bin/dd of=/dev/rmt/3hbn"

Recommendation is not to use absolute pathnames for directories in a
'tar' archive. Instead, use
./source_dir.


-to restore such backup:

cd /src_dir; ssh remote_host  "dd if=/dev/rmt/3hbn" | tar xvfp -


Hope this helps a bit.





